WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.952 --> 00:00:03.930
OpenCourseWare is
a web-based program

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:08.550
that will provide free access to
primary materials for virtually

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.800
every course at MIT.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.710
The founders of OCW had
a transformative vision

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.970
20 years ago of offering
access to materials

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.420
from the MIT classroom
openly, freely.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.550
They can learn from them
straight off the website.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.100
They can download them
and carry them around.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.070
They can remix them with
other kinds of materials

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.660
mash them up in new ways.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.420
They can share them
with their networks.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.940
We're getting about 22
million visits per year.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.430
We have more than 3
million subscribers

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.870
to the OCW YouTube channel.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:44.190
That makes it the biggest .edu
YouTube channel in the world.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.310
It has captured curious
learners of all stripes

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.900
from around the world.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.750
Several thousand MIT faculty
have shared materials

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.300
from more than 2,500 courses.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.400
We're sharing materials not just
from the science, technology,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.400
engineering, and math
courses and the management

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.770
courses that MIT
is most famous for,

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:06.900
but also from the incredible
richness of our humanities

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.360
and social sciences.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.150
The impact of OCW in opening
learning for millions

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.760
around the world is multiplied
by the role of educators

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.300
elsewhere.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.430
When they take
materials from OCW

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.560
and repurpose them and
use them and make them

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.620
part of their own teaching,
for each one educator that

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.050
does that, there are
dozens or hundreds

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.420
more people for whom the
opportunities to learn

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.400
are opened up.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.820
It takes resources to do
what we do at OpenCourseWare.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.780
It takes a lot of people and
time and energy and money

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.350
to cover the full
curriculum at MIT.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.350
We're right in the middle of
launching the program for OCW's

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.670
third decade.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.440
We're delighted that
we have now rolled

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.330
out its next-generation
platform.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:49.710
It's mobile friendly.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.600
It has much better search tools.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.850
What we teach it at
MIT changes with time.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.680
How we teach changes with time.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.720
And now we have a
new platform that

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.120
will allow us to keep
the content of OCW

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.460
current and vibrant
into the future.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.730
Knowledge should be
free, and especially

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:09.210
knowledge that comes from
leading institutions,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.880
institutions with the most
privilege behind them.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.280
To give that back to
the world has never

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.874
been more important than it is.

00:02:15.874 --> 00:02:17.810
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.840
So many of the challenges
that the world is facing

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.710
require the development, the
application, the testing,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.430
the refinement of new
forms of knowledge.

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:31.700
We firmly believe
that a world in which

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.400
the educational attainment
of millions of people

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.810
has been elevated will
be a better world.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:39.500
This is making a difference.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:42.250
[MUSIC PLAYING]

